00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.490
My mom was such a hard worker.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:52.036
- Yeah, and like doing a
million things at the same time.

00:01:52.036 --> 00:01:52.869
- [Kelly] Multitasking.

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:55.000
- You also like never
get away with anything

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.050
because there's no one to be like, well,

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.630
that parent said no, but
what about that parent?

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.420
My mom was like, no, I said no.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.690
- So where did you grow up?

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.860
- I grew up in Santa
Fe, New Mexico mostly.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.433
- Beautiful.

00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:10.247
- Yeah, it's a pretty
weird town, I have to say.

00:02:10.247 --> 00:02:11.440
- Is it? I love it.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.273
I visited, I love it.

00:02:12.273 --> 00:02:13.882
- Have you really?
- Yeah!

00:02:13.882 --> 00:02:14.715
- Oh, amazing.

00:02:14.715 --> 00:02:15.548
What did you do?

00:02:15.548 --> 00:02:17.548
- I was there because a
friend was shooting something

00:02:17.548 --> 00:02:20.430
and I was there for that reason.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.680
- Well what's so crazy is when
I was growing up, I was like,

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.330
I have to get out of
here, which now I'm like,

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.470
maybe that's more about teenagers

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:27.410
than actually about

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.660
where we grow up.
- 100%

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.480
- But yeah. I was like, I
have to get to the big city,

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.350
but now like all of these
film projects are filming

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:38.440
in New Mexico and I'm
like, this is so wild.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:42.000
Like my PE teacher works
in the film industry now.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.509
I'm like, well, that's cool.
- What?

00:02:44.509 --> 00:02:47.140
- Yeah, it's a big thing there now.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.010
- It's funny though, how we
wanna escape where we're from

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.310
and then all of a sudden, like,
all I crave is a small town.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.440
- Yeah, totally.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.722
- I love a small town.

00:02:53.722 --> 00:02:54.555
- And now I love going back home.

00:02:54.555 --> 00:02:58.420
And like, it has a totally
kind of eclectic art scene

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.910
and like George R.R. Martin
who wrote "Game of Thrones"

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.530
lives in Santa Fe, which
kind of gives you an insight.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.830
- And the shopping is awesome.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.610
You have such cool stores like antiques-

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.580
- Lots of turquoise.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.414
- Yes, I love turquoise.

00:03:10.414 --> 00:03:13.360
Well don't they have a crazy,

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.588
like the art scene.

00:03:14.588 --> 00:03:15.550
Were you always into that
like when you were a kid?

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.167
- Yeah.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.000
- Were you always artistic?

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:18.833
- Yeah, definitely.

00:03:18.833 --> 00:03:21.130
I definitely grew up and wanted to,

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:25.230
like loved being in
plays and I played piano

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.063
when I was young.

00:03:26.063 --> 00:03:27.780
I thought I was gonna be
like a concert pianist.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:28.620
- Oh, you were good.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.410
- Yeah, well, my mom, I think
when I was little noticed

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.860
I had like a lot of nervous
energy with my hands

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.690
and was like, "My
grandparents have a piano,

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.800
so we're just gonna put
her in piano lessons."

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.550
So I thought I was gonna
be like a classical pianist

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.860
until I was like, till I went to college.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.450
And then I kind of discovered
acting and realized,

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.840
all right, life choices.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.010
- Life choices.
(laughter)

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.750
- And I feel like your mind kind of like,

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.500
you kind of have weird goggles in New York

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.270
where you're like, I'm
sharing a one bedroom

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.744
with eight people, but it's amazing.

00:03:57.744 --> 00:03:58.911
(laughter)

00:03:58.911 --> 00:04:00.140
You're just like, this
is such a great deal!

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.370
And I like I shower in the
sink, but it's so great.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.970
- It's so fun.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.130
Well congrats on season
two of "Mr. Mayor".

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.641
This is awesome.

00:04:08.641 --> 00:04:09.702
- Thank you so much.

00:04:09.702 --> 00:04:10.535
- So for everybody that hasn't seen it,

00:04:10.535 --> 00:04:11.570
can you say who you play?

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:12.898
- Yes.

00:04:12.898 --> 00:04:16.320
So I play I'm Mikaela and I am
Ted Danson's chief of staff.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.775
So dream role and yeah,

00:04:19.775 --> 00:04:24.060
Ted Danson plays the mayor of
LA who like unexpectedly won

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.940
to impress his teenage daughter.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.680
And I play, I was his campaign manager

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:29.950
during the campaign.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:33.210
And then all of a sudden he
makes me his chief of staff.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.380
So like, Mikaela is
completely out of her depth.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.500
She's like never worked
in public office before

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.960
and she's running the
whole administration.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.302
So it's a really fun-

00:04:41.302 --> 00:04:42.444
- Terrifying,

00:04:42.444 --> 00:04:43.277
it's terrifying.
- Yeah, it's terrifying.

00:04:43.277 --> 00:04:44.410
Yeah, totally.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.940
It's a fun character to play though.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.870
